, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. The release history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc as unhealthy; the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0. checkout-api was rolled back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. After the rollback the service reports healthy, with an error rate of 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52116, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01SpLmTeBRihz3C1u1nPiL3z", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52116, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SpLmTeBRihz3C1u1nPiL3z", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 56165, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. v2.3.0 was the most recent release marked healthy; both v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were unhealthy. After the rollback, the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is a SEV2 for checkout-api. It covers the failing release, the rollback, the current health, and a follow-up to find what broke in v2.3.1 before it's deployed again. The first request to create it timed out. I checked that no incident existed yet, then sent it again with the same duplicate-prevention key, so only one incident was opened.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011FH3LzxCh3NwdJf1jyBT6K", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"